From: Benjamin Kelenyi <benjamin@wendy.sh>
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "usb: dwc3: qcom: Add support to skip phy management by USB core"

The managed software node this adds is freed once too often when dwc3
tears the xHCI down to change role, so the first unplug from an OTG port
reports "refcount_t: underflow; use-after-free" and leaves the controller
bound to neither role -- no xHCI and no UDC -- until the next boot.

  refcount_warn_saturate
   kobject_put
    software_node_notify_remove
     device_del / usb_disconnect / usb_remove_hcd / xhci_plat_remove
  Workqueue: events_freezable __dwc3_set_mode

Only a port that actually switches role reaches this, so it needs a
connector that drives the role switch.

The cost is that usb-core resumes managing the dwc3 node's own HS/SS
PHYs: without xhci-skip-phy-init-quirk, usb_add_hcd() allocates a PHY
roothub from the same "phys" phandles dwc3 already init/exits, on every
role switch. The upstream revert also drops the property.h include; this
tree still calls device_property_read_bool(), so that hunk is omitted.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [revert of be7b1c68cd3e ("usb: dwc3: qcom: Add
support to skip phy management by USB core"); posted on linux-arm-msm and
Acked-by Thinh Nguyen. Drop this file once the revert reaches the pinned
kernel.]

Signed-off-by: Benjamin Kelenyi <benjamin@wendy.sh>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c | 14 --------------
 1 file changed, 14 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c
@@ -448,16 +448,6 @@ static irqreturn_t qcom_dwc3_resume_irq(int irq, void *data)
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }

-static int dwc3_qcom_set_swnode(struct device *dev)
-{
-	const struct property_entry props[] = {
-		PROPERTY_ENTRY_BOOL("xhci-skip-phy-init-quirk"),
-		{}
-	};
-
-	return device_create_managed_software_node(dev, props, NULL);
-}
-
 static void dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk(struct dwc3_qcom *qcom)
 {
 	/* Configure dwc3 to use UTMI clock as PIPE clock not present */
@@ -735,10 +725,6 @@ static int dwc3_qcom_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ignore_pipe_clk)
 		dwc3_qcom_select_utmi_clk(qcom);

-	ret = dwc3_qcom_set_swnode(dev);
-	if (ret)
-		goto clk_disable;
-
 	qcom->mode = usb_get_dr_mode(dev);

 	if (qcom->mode == USB_DR_MODE_HOST) {
